@slin1237 could you help land this once the baseline CI completes? @AgainstEntropy and @JustinTong0323 have approved.

I corrected the commit attribution to my personal GitHub identity; the full source tree is unchanged from the reviewed head `b4f58fd6`. Local Anthropic tests (73 tests, 30 subtests) and applicable pre-commit hooks pass.

The previous [Xeon run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40916188702/job/123597205405) failed in `test_cpu_graph.py` with `TreeCacheNamespace` missing `req_to_token_pool`, outside the changed Anthropic path. I have not reproduced it on clean main; could you assess that failure and merge when ready?

